// AUTO-GENERATED reference data -- do not hand-edit column lists without
// re-checking against db/schema.sql + schema_additions_*.sql. Regenerate with:
//   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "select table_name, column_name from information_schema.columns where table_schema='public' ..."
//
// This is the allowlist that closes the SQL-injection vulnerability in the
// "generic upsert" pattern used across mutations.functions.ts,
// capability-api.functions.ts, field-*.functions.ts, production-*.functions.ts,
// and template-mutations.functions.ts: those files build UPDATE/INSERT
// statements by interpolating client-supplied JSON keys directly into SQL
// as column identifiers. Table names were already allowlisted; column names
// were not. This file provides that missing allowlist.
//
// IMPORTANT: 'id', 'created_at', 'updated_at' are deliberately excluded from
// every table below -- they're either the row identifier (handled separately
// by every call site's WHERE clause) or timestamps Postgres triggers
// maintain automatically. Never add them back without checking why a call
// site would need to set them from client input.

